 {
  "id": "sg-art-se",
  "type": "section",
  "settings": { "style": "default", "width": "small", "padding": "small", "padding_top": 56, "padding_bottom": 56 },
  "style": { "bg": { "type": "solid", "color": "var(--olo-color-background)" } },
  "advanced": {},
  "children": [
   {
    "id": "sg-art-ro",
    "type": "row",
    "settings": {},
    "style": {},
    "advanced": {},
    "children": [
     {
      "id": "sg-art-co",
      "type": "column",
      "settings": { "width": "1-1" },
      "style": {},
      "advanced": {},
      "children": [
       {
        "id": "sg-art-kicker",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>// systems · debugging</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-primary)",
         "font_size": "12",
         "line_height": "1.4",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 14, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-h1",
        "type": "headline",
        "settings": {
         "heading": "The cache that lied to us for three months",
         "tag": "h1",
         "alignment": "left",
         "heading_font": "heading",
         "heading_font_size": "52",
         "heading_line_height": "1.06",
         "heading_font_weight": "600",
         "heading_color": "#eef2ec",
         "decoration": "none"
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-meta",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>by Devin Cho · 14 min read · updated 2 days ago</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text-muted)",
         "font_size": "12.5",
         "line_height": "1.4",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": { "margin_top": 18, "padding_bottom": 0, "margin_bottom": 0 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-cover",
        "type": "workgrid",
        "settings": {
         "columns": 1,
         "items_gap": 0,
         "media_aspect": "16/9",
         "media_tall_aspect": "4/5",
         "media_bg": "#1a212a",
         "media_label_color": "#eef2ec",
         "hover_zoom": false,
         "title_font_family": "heading",
         "title_color": "#eef2ec",
         "title_size": 20,
         "title_weight": "600",
         "meta_color": "var(--olo-color-primary)",
         "meta_size": 11,
         "show_desc": false,
         "desc_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
         "desc_size": 13,
         "mono_font_family": "IBM Plex Mono",
         "items": [
          { "image": "", "media_label": "cover diagram — read path with a stale node", "title": "", "meta": "", "description": "", "link_url": "", "tall": false }
         ]
        },
        "style": { "margin_top": 30, "margin_bottom": 36 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-p1",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>It started, as these things do, with a graph that looked too good. Our p99 read latency had dropped off a cliff in March and stayed there. We congratulated ourselves on the new caching layer and moved on. We should not have moved on.</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
         "font_size": "18",
         "line_height": "1.8",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 22, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-h3a",
        "type": "headline",
        "settings": {
         "heading": "# The symptom",
         "tag": "h3",
         "alignment": "left",
         "heading_font": "heading",
         "heading_font_size": "24",
         "heading_font_weight": "600",
         "heading_color": "#eef2ec",
         "decoration": "none"
        },
        "style": { "margin_top": 34, "margin_bottom": 14 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-p2",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>Three months later, support started seeing reports of users seeing <code>old</code> data — profile changes that \"didn't save\", settings that reverted. Intermittent, unreproducible, maddening. The writes were succeeding. The reads were just… wrong.</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
         "font_size": "18",
         "line_height": "1.8",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 22, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-p3",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>The cache wasn't slow. It was <em>confident</em>. And it was confidently serving stale values because of a single line:</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
         "font_size": "18",
         "line_height": "1.8",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 22, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-code",
        "type": "code",
        "settings": {
         "code": "// cache.ts — the line that cost us a quarter\nconst ttl = process.env.CACHE_TTL ?? 86400;  // seconds\n// CACHE_TTL was unset in prod → 24h TTL, never invalidated on write",
         "language": "typescript",
         "theme": "github-dark",
         "show_line_numbers": false,
         "show_copy_button": true,
         "font_size": "13.5",
         "wrap_lines": false
        },
        "style": { "margin_bottom": 24 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-h3b",
        "type": "headline",
        "settings": {
         "heading": "# The fix, and the lesson",
         "tag": "h3",
         "alignment": "left",
         "heading_font": "heading",
         "heading_font_size": "24",
         "heading_font_weight": "600",
         "heading_color": "#eef2ec",
         "decoration": "none"
        },
        "style": { "margin_top": 34, "margin_bottom": 14 },
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-p4",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>The fix was trivial: invalidate on write, and fail loudly when a config the system depends on is missing. The lesson was not. A metric that only ever looks good is not a metric — it's a blind spot with a dashboard.</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
         "font_size": "18",
         "line_height": "1.8",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 22, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       },
       {
        "id": "sg-art-p5",
        "type": "text-block",
        "settings": {
         "content": "<p>We now treat \"suspiciously good\" the same way we treat \"suspiciously bad\": as something to investigate before we trust it.</p>",
         "text_color": "var(--olo-color-text)",
         "font_size": "18",
         "line_height": "1.8",
         "text_align": "left",
         "tile_padding": { "top": 0, "right": 0, "bottom": 0, "left": 0 }
        },
        "style": {},
        "advanced": {},
        "children": []
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
